      "updated": 1792480177904,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. LinkedList is a linear data structure .\n\n2. It does't require contigious memory to store data .\n\n3. It collection NODES. \n\n4. Node is combination of 2 things :\n -> data : to store value .\n ->  next : to store address of next node .\n\n5. Thus each node is connceted vio internal pointer called as\nnext .",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. LinkedList is a linear data structure .\n\n2. It does't require contigious memory to store data .\n\n3. It collection NODES. \n\n4. Node is combination of 2 things :\n -> data : to store value .\n ->  next : to store address of next node .\n\n5. Thus each node is connceted vio internal pointer called as next .",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
